An embedder's vkGetInstanceProcAddr for the Vulkan backend (Minato's ADR-0044, decision 3; ADR-0029, decision 8).

Why: Minato's graphics/host stands in front of MoltenVK for ANGLE's instance (the private API's setting, the queues
for "scheduled", the background gate), so ANGLE must reach Vulkan through graphics/host's vkGetInstanceProcAddr and
never open a loader past it. ANGLEVulkanSetGetInstanceProcAddr, named like patch 0003's ANGLEMetalSetCommitGates,
takes it before the first Vulkan display; once it was called, the renderer skips OpenLibVulkan and hands it to
volkInitializeCustom. The checkout keeps no Vulkan loader, so angle_vulkan_entry_points names the loader's target
only when ANGLE builds its own (angle_use_custom_libvulkan), as angle_libvulkan does.
Upstream: not proposed; it is Minato's hook into the backend.
Remove: never while graphics/host stands in front of MoltenVK for ANGLE.

